{1}{G:}{G:}{}{}{}{}
{2}{Greetings, sir. My name is @PCNAME@. Are you the owner of this plantation?}{}{5}{me 0}{5}{}
{3}{Uh.... Hi dere! Me @PCNAME@ Who are yuu?}{}{-4}{me 0}{5}{}
{3}{Hello again, Mr. Yoki. May I speak with you a moment?}{}{5}{me 1}{62}{}
{4}{Hi dere, Mr. Yoki. Yuu gots a moment?}{}{-4}{me 1}{62}{}
{5}{I am Mr. Yoki Tagemie, and welcome to Plainwicke Plantation.  I hope you have plenty of extra men outside, oh and, did my boys explain the situation throughly enough so you know what you're getting into? }{I am Mr. Yoki Tagemie, and welcome to Plainwicke Plantation. How may I be of service, madam?}{}{}{}{}
{6}{[You smile] Like I told your man outside, I wasn't hired to come here.  I was just passing through and noticed the felled trees, then chatted with the fellow out front.}{1}{5}{}{10}{}
{7}{ I was just passing through and noticed the felled trees, then chatted with the fellow out front. You people seem to be in a dreadful fix.}{0}{5}{}{17}{}
{8}{Me wuz just out seein' da sights when me seen da trees and stopped to talk to da man out front. Sounds like yuu got trubble.}{1}{-4}{}{300}{}
{9}{Me wuz just out seein' da sights when me seen da trees and stopped to talk to da man out front. Sounds like yuu got trubble.}{0}{-4}{}{300}{}
{10}{Please accept my most sincere appologies, sir. I simply made the wrong assumption about you.}{Please accept my most sincere appologies, sir. I simply made the wrong assumption about you.}{}{}{}{}
{11}{There's nothing to appologise for, Mr. Yoki. Under these circumstances, I believe I would have came to the same conclusion.}{}{5}{}{14}{re +5}
{12}{I believe I can let it pass, this time.}{}{5}{}{14}{re -5}
{13}{}{}{}{}{}{}
{14}{Thank you. Are you on holiday or dare I hope that you are an adventurer seeking a new challenge?}{Thank you. Are you on holiday or dare I hope that you are an adventurer seeking a new challenge?}{}{}{}{}
{15}{I'm just being a tourist today, thank you. }{1}{5}{}{17}{}
{16}{I seem to have become quite the adventurer lately, and I heard you folks are having a spot of trouble. Some sort of magick spiders?}{1}{5}{}{22}{}
{17}{In that case, sir, I don't mean to seem rude, but I really cannot spare the time to chat with you. You'll find the windmill at the north end of the enclosure, and Artie at the northwest gate. He can answer any questions you may have. Good day to you.}{Yes, we are. Madam, I don't mean to seem rude, but I really cannot spare the time to chat with you. You'll find the windmill at the north end of the enclosure, and Artie at the northwest gate. He can answer any questions you may have. Good day to you.}{}{}{}{}
{18}{As you wish. Perhaps we'll speak again, at a more opportune time.}{}{5}{}{0}{fl 21}
{19}{A moment more, please. I spoke with Red and I believe I might be of some assistance in your dilemma. Some sort of magick spiders?}{}{5}{}{22}{}
{29}{[Her eyes go hard] No! Are YOU lookin' for trouble, mister? I'm in the mood to give you all you can handle and then some!}{[Her eyes go hard] No! Are YOU lookin' for trouble, missy? I'm in the mood to give you all you want and then some!}{}{}{}{}
{21}{[He smiles, nods, and returns to paperwork]}{[He smiles, nods, and returns to paperwork]}{}{}{}{}
{22}{Magick spiders, indeed! Blasted monstrosities! We lost three good men to those things, but we've got them contained. }{Magick spiders, indeed! Blasted monstrosities! We lost three good men to those things, but we've got them contained. }{}{}{}{}
{23}{But fur how much longer?}{}{-4}{}{25}{}
{24}{But for how much longer?}{}{5}{}{25}{}
{25}{[He sighs] That is a very good question. If help doesn't arrive soon, one of three things are going to happen - The streams will become shallow enough for them to escape, I'll have to order the old mill to be torn apart to keep the fires going, or we'll have to grab what we can and abandon Plainwicke. I really do not like the sound of any of those.}{[He sighs] That is a very good question. If help doesn't arrive soon, one of three things are going to happen - The streams will become shallow enough for them to escape, I'll have to order the old mill to be torn apart to keep the fires going, or we'll have to grab what we can and abandon Plainwicke. I really do not like the sound of any of those.}{}{}{}{}
{26}{Why don't we add a fourth option? A passing stranger accepts the task of slaying the creatures while they are still confined.}{}{5}{}{35}{}
{27}{Dere is one more ting - Sumone comes to farm and kills da spiders while dey are still trapped.}{}{-4}{}{35}{}
{28}{I really sorry but the more I hear of this, the less I like it. I would withdraw my offer of assistance, if I may, and wish you all the best of luck.}{}{5}{}{30}{}
{29}{Me sorry, but me not likin' sound of dis. Me want outta offer to help but me wish yuu gud luck.}{}{-4}{}{30}{}
{30}{In that case, sir, I have matters to attend to. I assume you can find the door. Good day.}{In that case, madam, I have matters to attend to. I assume you can find the door. Good day.}{}{}{}{re -5}
{31}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{35}{OH! Dare I hope?}{OH! Dare I hope?}{}{}{}{}
{36}{There is always hope, Mr. Tagamie. I believe I am up to this challenge, however... At the risk of sounding crass, what is the pay?}{}{5}{}{40}{}
{37}{Dere is always hope, Mr. Tag-ah-me. Me can do dis, but me cannot work fur free. Sorry. Whut is da pay?}{}{-4}{}{40}{}
